 little' (2), 'Quite a bit' (3) and 'Very much' (4). For the remaining 2 questions the response is requested on a 7-point scale from 1 ('Very poor') to 7 ('Excellent'). The raw scale scores were linear transformed, producing scale scores that ranged from 0% to 100%. A high scale score represents a higher response level. Hence for the functional scales and the global health status a higher score indicates a better QoL, whilst for the symptom scale scores this is implied by a lower score.","populationDescription":"The ITT set included all randomized subjects.","reportingStatus":"POSTED","paramType":"MEAN","dispersionType":"Standard Deviation","unitOfMeasure":"Score on a scale","timeFrame":"Week 17 and Week 48","groups":[{"id":"OG000","title":"Open-label Period: Continue Pegcetacoplan","description":"On Day 1 of the RCP, the subjects were randomized to receive monotherapy with SC infusions of pegcetacoplan 1080 mg twice-weekly or every 3 days up to the end of the open-label period (Week 48)."},{"id":"OG001","title":"Open-label Period: Crossover to Pegcetacoplan","description":"Subjects entered the open-label run-in period where they received pegcetacoplan 1080 mg twice-weekly in addition to eculizumab for 4 weeks (Week 17 to Week 20) before receiving monotherapy with SC infusions of pegcetacoplan 1080 mg twice-weekly or every 3 days up to the end of the open-label period (Week 48)."}],"denoms":[{"units":"Participants","counts":[{"groupId":"OG000","value":"30"},{"groupId":"OG001","value":"26"}]}],"classes":[{"title":"Global Health Status/QoL","categories":[{"measurements":[{"groupId":"OG000","value":"7.22","spread":"19.664"},{"groupId":"OG001","value":"23.08","spread":"22.149"}]}]},{"title":"Functional Scales - Physical functioning","categories":[{"measurements":[{"groupId":"OG000","value":"0.89","spread":"10.168"},{"groupId":"OG001","value":"11.03","spread":"17.173"}]}]},{"title":"Functional Scales - Role functioning","categories":[{"measurements":[{"groupId":"OG000","